{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531084-breaking-the-chains-of-shyness-with-vampire-the-masquerade","id":1531084,"title":"Breaking the chains of shyness!... With Vampire the Masquerade.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-18T19:35:28-08:00","id":1531084,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Breaking the chains of shyness!... With Vampire the Masquerade.","content":"Hey there.<br /> I love Vampire - The Masquerade, ever since playing it for the first time. The lore, the gothic-punk ambience, the darkness in the world (yeah, that's right), and Jason Carl. But ever since playing it for the first time, I got to actually play it only twice. One in which I created my absolute favorite character of all time, and I'm currently playing another more casual campaign now, in which my wife is the Storyteller. For three years since I've known this saga, I've only got the chance of being the Storyteller myself, even earning the title &quot;Malkavian Mind&quot; from my friends, due to the complex plots and characters I've come to develop and love.<br /> <br /> But I've been craving for being a player for SO LONG. Gladly, Vampire the Masquerade has a really wonderful set of fans and players all around the world, and with today's technology the accessibility to that only grows. Cue Discord and stuff for example. Thing is... I'm an awkward piece of shyness. With my friends I'm a totally different person, but with strangers it tends to freeze me in a state of monosyllabic responses, even despite wanting to say much much more. I've recently been diagnosed with autism, much from the encouragement of my wife to actually look further into it (we're both Psychologists) and suddenly the whole world makes sense to me LOL. I don't want to go pointing fingers at the condition and using it as crutches, but boy oh boy, does that awkwardness of constantly thinking about acting and socializing in what I judge to be the expected way kill me.<br /> <br /> I'd really really like to start playing with other people, even through Discord, because I really really miss playing it, and not storytelling it. I'm hungry for the story other people have to tell, to be surprised, to be shocked, to be on the receiving end for once, but every time I think about joining a server which has a chronicle about to start, I freeze at the thought of having to stare at a computer and talk to people I can't even see.<br /> <br /> So my good friends, could you help me? Do you know of any group of players who are willing to go the extra mile of patient to deal with someone like me? Do you have any tips for me myself?<br /> Anything is welcome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","user":"TravisLegge","date":".  Edited to remove the use of a slur. Please see Rule 1. Consider this a warning to avoid such language. 02-19-2024, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28353-nicknickeo","name":"NickNickeo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28353_4.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-20T04:40:48-08:00","id":1531186,"title":"","content":"Hi, I recall discord is probably the best place to pick games up","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T01:14:00-07:00","id":1536951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NickNickeo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531084-breaking-the-chains-of-shyness-with-vampire-the-masquerade#post1531084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey there.<br /> I love Vampire - The Masquerade, ever since playing it for the first time. The lore, the gothic-punk ambience, the darkness in the world (yeah, that's right), and Jason Carl. But ever since playing it for the first time, I got to actually play it only twice. One in which I created my absolute favorite character of all time, and I'm currently playing another more casual campaign now, in which my wife is the Storyteller. For three years since I've known this saga, I've only got the chance of being the Storyteller myself, even earning the title &quot;Malkavian Mind&quot; from my friends, due to the complex plots and characters I've come to develop and love.<br /> <br /> But I've been craving for being a player for SO LONG. Gladly, Vampire the Masquerade has a really wonderful set of fans and players all around the world, and with today's technology the accessibility to that only grows. Cue Discord and stuff for example. Thing is... I'm an awkward piece of shyness. With my friends I'm a totally different person, but with strangers it tends to freeze me in a state of monosyllabic responses, even despite wanting to say much much more. I've recently been diagnosed with autism, much from the encouragement of my wife to actually look further into it (we're both Psychologists) and suddenly the whole world makes sense to me LOL. I don't want to go pointing fingers at the condition and using it as crutches, but boy oh boy, does that awkwardness of constantly thinking about acting and socializing in what I judge to be the expected way kill me.<br /> <br /> I'd really really like to start playing with other people, even through Discord, because I really really miss playing it, and not storytelling it. I'm hungry for the story other people have to tell, to be surprised, to be shocked, to be on the receiving end for once, but every time I think about joining a server which has a chronicle about to start, I freeze at the thought of having to stare at a computer and talk to people I can't even see.<br /> <br /> So my good friends, could you help me? Do you know of any group of players who are willing to go the extra mile of patient to deal with someone like me? Do you have any tips for me myself?<br /> Anything is welcome!</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like you would probably enjoy the romantic aspect of popular vampirism, Anne Rice vampires, so you would probably like playing as a Toreador. Try to find a Game Master who doesn't run Vtm as D&amp;D With Fangs. Good luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}